{"name":"Light of New Hope","hex":"#eaf3d0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"new","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Newar."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Recently made, or created.","Of recent origin; having taken place recently."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/new"},{"term":"hope","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To want (something) to happen, with a sense of expectation that it might .mw-parser-output .object-usage-tag{font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output .deprecated{color:var(--wikt-palette-grey-lime-8,olivedrab)}[with that (+ clause); or  with clause; or with so or  not].","To intend to do something and look forward to the prospect of having done it [with to (+ infinitive)]."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The feeling of trust, confidence, belief or expectation that something wished for can or will happen.","The actual thing wished for."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hope"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hope","blocks":[{"text":"Hope is an optimistic state of mind that is based on an expectation of desirable outcomes with respect to events and circumstances in one's own life, or the world at large. As a verb, Merriam-Webster defines hope as \"to expect with confidence\" or \"to cherish a desire with anticipation\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Hopeful.jpg/330px-Hopeful.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","lin